.TH "SCCFM-CLI INVENTORY DEVICES ASA LIST-NOT-ON-VERSION" "1" "2026-08-26" "0.40.0" "sccfm-cli inventory devices asa list-not-on-version Manual"
.SH NAME
sccfm-cli\-inventory\-devices\-asa\-list-not-on-version \- List ASA devices that are NOT running a...
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sccfm-cli inventory devices asa list-not-on-version
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List ASA devices that are NOT running a specific software version. Useful for identifying devices that still need upgrading to a target version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fP TEXT
Software version to exclude (e.g. '9.20(3)13'). Devices NOT on this version are listed.  [required]
.TP
\fB\-n,\fP \-\-device\-name TEXT
Device name to search for (supports wildcards like 'branch-*').
.TP
\fB\-q,\fP \-\-query TEXT
Lucene query to narrow the device search (combined with the version exclusion filter).
.TP
\fB\-l,\fP \-\-limit INTEGER RANGE
Maximum records to return  [default: 50; 1<=x<=200]
.TP
\fB\-o,\fP \-\-offset INTEGER RANGE
Pagination offset  [default: 0; x>=0]
.TP
\fB\-u,\fP \-\-device\-uids TEXT
List of device UIDs to query.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fP [table|json]
Output format  [default: table]
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-path\fP PATH
Path to the configuration file (defaults to ~/.sccfm-cli/config.json).
